# Reserved channels: what is said there never leaves, and the name itself is
# never written anywhere else (leak_guard.py). Copy to `bot.reserved` (or point
# BOT_RESERVED at it) and keep it out of the repo: the file names the channels
# it protects.
#
# `<irc host> <#channel>`, one per line, the host exactly as the instance that
# sits in the channel has it in IRC_HOST. Every instance reads the same file,
# so a name listed here is blocked on all networks. Whole-line comments only:
# a trailing `# ...` cannot be told apart from a channel name.
irc.example.net #secret
